.TH HOSTS 1 2026-07-26 "hosts @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
hosts \- a safe command\-line manager for /etc/hosts
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hosts
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B hosts
.BR \-h | \-\-help
.br
.B hosts
.BR \-V | \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hosts
manages the entries of the system hosts file without opening it in an
editor.
The hosts file is critical for name resolution, so every write is performed
on a temporary file in the same directory, validated, and then moved into
place with an atomic rename, preserving owner, group and permissions.
.PP
This release provides the packaging and build scaffolding only.
No entry management command is implemented yet.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a usage summary and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the program version and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/hosts
The static table of hostname to IP address mappings that
.B hosts
is designed to manage.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Exit codes are part of the public interface and keep their meaning for the
whole 1.x release line.
Values greater than or equal to 64 are reserved and never returned.
.TP
.B 0
Success, including an idempotent operation that changed nothing.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error: unknown command, unknown option, or a missing argument.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hosts (5),
.BR hostname (7),
.BR getent (1)
.PP
Full documentation is available on
.UR https://n36l3c7.github.io/hosts-cli/
the project website
.UE .
.SH AUTHORS
Samuele Gervasio
